{
  "description": "The impact walk of the tom_specs change mode (spec_impact_walk): for every document root of the model, in model order, one row per class node (root, complex, section, list item), one per list (with its item count) and, for an empty list of a class element, one template row `<list>/*` with that class's subtree; each row with its section-id chain (a list item by its stored id), class, depth, filled (hasValuesUnder), values (content leaves plus form-field values at or below the path), items, and CodeSpecs routing (the class's; a list: its element class's, or for a list of scalars the field-level @CodeSpecKind, else the owner class's; below a feedsProcess section that section's routing). A class already on the branch is not entered again. A root without a document is walked over an empty one and is `present: false`. level is specImpactLevel over the case's listing, tests and code folders; documentFiles is specImpactDocumentFiles over the listing; markdown is specImpactWalkMarkdown(walk, level). A case's `model` is `model.meta.json` or an inline model; a document is a corpus state file name or an inline state, keyed by root type. Every runtime that carries spec_impact_walk runs every case.",
